  "name": "Barbarian Adept",
  "type": "feat",
  "img": "icons/magic/symbols/question-stone-yellow.webp",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You fight with powerful and reckless abandon, able to smash through any challenge. You gain the following benefits:</p><ul><li>Increase your Strength or Constitution by 1, to a maximum of 20.</li><li>As a bonus action, you can enter a fighting frenzy that lasts until the start of your next turn. During this frenzy, your weapon attacks made with Strength deal an additional 2 damage, and you gain a +2 bonus to Strength checks and saving throws. You can use this feature two times, regaining all uses at the end of a long rest.</li><li>When you make your first attack on your turn, you can decide to attack recklessly. Doing so gives you advantage on melee weapon attack rolls using Strength during this turn, but attack rolls against you have advantage until your next turn.</li></ul>",
      "chat": ""
    },
